Z||000008||theogre||06-06-2001||09:05 PM||||All the rust has to go.<P>I'd use metal. Fiberglass has a nasty habit of cracking off metal, especially in areas with big temperature swings.<P>Sand the rusted section to bare metal.<BR>Cut a patch to overlap 3/4 to one inch.<P>Unless you have a body shop access, you basically have 2 attachment options.<P>1. coat the bare metal with a sealer. Something that will be thick and gooey. Roofing mastic works really well for this and it's tougher that undercoating. Then rivit the patch down while the mastic is wet. This will seal the joint so nothing starts more rust. Once the patch is installed, coat it with the mastic on both sides. Make sure you cover all the rivits good.<P>2. Epoxy the patch in place. Messy but you don't have to drill. then coat all bare areas with roof mastic or undercoating to protect them.||||reg||1
